# libFuzzer's own runtime allocates at exit in ways LSan flags but that are not
# under-test code: the RSS-monitor std::thread is heap-allocated and never joined
# (fuzzer::StartRssThread), and the coverage/PC printer allocates in the symbolizer
# when new PCs are observed. Both stacks are entirely inside fuzzer:: internals with
# the parser nowhere on them. Suppress the whole libFuzzer runtime so detect_leaks=1
# stays live for CommandSerializer/ByteMagic (their frames never contain "fuzzer::").
leak:fuzzer::
